# Cloudflare static assets always strips `.html` from a URL — no html_handling
# value serves /live_streaming_apps.html directly, so the canonical URL for the
# app page had to become /live_streaming_apps/ on the move off Vercel.
# This makes the old indexed URL a permanent redirect so Google consolidates it
# instead of treating the target as a separate page. Without the rule the
# built-in handler still redirects, but as a 307 (temporary), which does not.
/live_streaming_apps.html  /live_streaming_apps/  301
